     which has the side effect of deleting it again.  Note: this seems to cause
     instability, nonrepeatable particle deposition errors, and crashes after the
     fluid main loop.
    
     The scalar fields computed from the particle positions are now module-wide
     variables that can be used elsewhere in the code. p_i_par and p_i_perp are
     the parallel and perpendicular components of the hot ion pressure tensor
     respectively.
    
     The delta-f method has been switched on by default, and a new routine,
     define_phot0() has been written to compute the pressure due to the f0
     particle distribution, which is stored in new field p_hot0.
    
     A slowing-down f0 distribution has been added as an option in evalf0().
    
     A diagnostic routine, samplefield(), has been added to support debugging.

