    Changes to particle.f90:
    
     In advance_particles(), replaced potentially deadlocking MPI_Sendrecv()
     calls for particle exchange between domains with non-blocking
     MPI_Isend() / MPI_Irecv() pairs.  Fixed a serious bug in which particles
     received from different domains were written to the same location in the
     same buffer, resulting in unpredictable data loss.
    
     In init_particles, increased max ion energy from 1 keV to a more realistic
     10 keV; allowed for initial particle distribution to span multiple toroidal
     angles; and corrected Jacobian to keep distribution uniform in real space.
     Increased particle count to max of 245760.
    
     Fixed bug in particle_test that printed undefined time values to the first
     line of the trajectory trace file. Added time value to screen output.
    
     Increased sample time step size in particle_test to better reflect expected
     fluid step sizes; decreased step count for quicker testing with large
     particle populations.
    
     Optimized delete_particle() routine by replacing expensive circular memory
     shift call with the simple replacement of the single deleted element by the
     entry at the end of the list.
    
     Modified particle search in init_particles to use previously found host
     element as initial guess for next to cut initialization time.
    
     Replaced some MPI_Allreduce() calls with MPI_reduce() to cut down on
     communication.
    
     Improved normalization of pressure component integrals in
     particle_pressure().
    
     Modified init_ndlookup to print domain neighbor info only in debug mode.

